{"type":"standard","title":"Vayu language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Vayu language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7917585","titles":{"canonical":"Vayu_language","normalized":"Vayu language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Vayu language</span></span>"},"pageid":17782135,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1328933710","tid":"c7797b89-df5f-11f0-b7e7-f8067a50a5f4","timestamp":"2025-12-22T17:58:11Z","description":"Sino-Tibetan language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayu_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayu_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayu_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Vayu_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayu_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Vayu_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayu_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Vayu_language"}},"extract":"Vayu (वायु), also known as Wayu or Hayu (हायु) is a Sino-Tibetan language spoken in Nepal by about 1,520 people in Bagmati Province. Dialects include Pali Gau, Mudajor, Sukajor, Ramechhap, Sindhuli, and Marin Khola.","extract_html":"<p><b>Vayu</b> (वायु), also known as <b>Wayu</b> or <b>Hayu</b> (हायु) is a Sino-Tibetan language spoken in Nepal by about 1,520 people in Bagmati Province. Dialects include Pali Gau, Mudajor, Sukajor, Ramechhap, Sindhuli, and Marin Khola.</p>"}